| **C – “progressive‑thrust policy”** | **+93.8** | The car receives a modest forward thrust ( +0.6 ) while it is still on the left side of the valley, then a stronger thrust ( +0.8 ) once it has passed the centre (p ≈ 0.30). The rule *“if velocity is negative and we are already a little to the right of the centre, push forward (+0.8)”* prevents the car from stalling on the right slope. The episode finishes just after the car reaches the goal (p ≈ 0.45) and the 100‑point bonus outweighs the small action‑penalty.  

**Conclusion:**  
