#  Mountain‑Car progressive thrust controller (v2)
# --------------------------------------------------------------

IF p >= 0.45                               THEN a = 0.0                # goal reached
ELIF p >= 0.30 AND v > 0.05                THEN a = 0.6                # we are on the right slope, already fast
ELIF p >= 0.30 AND v > 0.00                THEN a = 0.8                # still need a strong push
ELIF p >= 0.30 AND v <= 0.00               THEN a = 0.8                # we slipped back, push forward again
ELIF p > 0.00 AND v < 0.00                 THEN a = 0.8                # negative velocity after centre → recover
ELIF p > -0.20 AND v > 0.04                THEN a = 0.7                # modest forward thrust in the left valley
ELIF p > -0.20 AND v <= 0.04               THEN a = 0.6                # keep building speed gently
ELIF p <= -0.20 AND v < 0.02               THEN a = 0.7                # extra boost when we are far left & almost stopped
ELIF p <= -0.20 AND v >= 0.00              THEN a = -0.8               # we are moving right but still too far left → brake a little
ELSE                                        a = 0.6                # default forward thrust
```

**Explanation of the branches**

| Branch | When it fires | Why it is useful |
|--------|---------------|------------------|
| `p >= 0.45` | Goal reached | No more force is needed; we stop to avoid the action penalty. |
| `p >= 0.30 & v > 0.05` | On the right hill, already fast | We can afford to **reduce** the thrust to 0.6 – the car will still crest the hill but we save the ‑0.1·a² penalty. |
| `p >= 0.30 & v > 0.00` | Right hill, still accelerating | Full forward push (0.8) gives the extra momentum needed to cross the summit. |
| `p >= 0.30 & v <= 0.00` | We have slipped back on the right side | A strong forward push (0.8) quickly restores positive velocity. |
| `p > 0.00 & v < 0.00` | Slightly right of centre but moving left | Same as above – push forward hard. |
| `p > -0.20 & v > 0.04` | Still in the left valley, already gaining speed | A *moderate* thrust (0.7) is enough; we avoid the extra penalty of 0.8 while still building kinetic energy. |
| `p > -0.20 & v <= 0.04` | Left valley, still slow | Use 0.6 – a gentle nudge that keeps the car from stalling. |
| `p <= -0.20 & v < 0.02` | Very far left and almost stopped | The car would otherwise waste many steps climbing out; a slightly larger thrust (0.7) gets it moving again. |
| `p <= -0.20 & v >= 0.00` | Far left but already moving right | Apply a small *brake* (‑0.8) to keep the car from overshooting into the opposite valley; this is rarely used because the previous rule usually gives enough forward push. |
| `ELSE` | Catch‑all | Default forward thrust (0.6) – safe fallback. |

