## Updated rule‑based policy (the one we will adopt)

The new policy keeps the spirit of the best strategy but adds two refinements:

1. **A smoother taper of forward force when approaching the goal** – we step down from 0.5 → 0.3 → 0.0 as the position increases.
2. **A “brake‑when‑still‑going‑fast” clause** – if the car is already moving fast (|v| > 0.07) and is close to the goal, we cut the thrust to 0.0 to avoid the quadratic action penalty.

```text
IF    p >= 0.45                               THEN a = 0.0                # goal reached
ELIF  p >= 0.40  AND v > 0.00                  THEN a = 0.3                # gentle push near top
ELIF  p >= 0.35  AND v > 0.00                  THEN a = 0.5                # mid‑hill boost
ELIF  p >= 0.30  AND v > 0.00                  THEN a = 0.6                # early climb
ELIF  v > 0.00                                 THEN a = 0.6                # any positive speed left of 0.30
ELIF  v <= 0.00  AND p > -0.20                 THEN a = -0.8               # slow down on the right side of the valley
ELIF  p <= -0.20                               THEN a = -1.0               # max left thrust in deep valley
ELIF  v > 0.00  AND p <= -0.20                 THEN a = 0.6                # push right when already heading right
ELSE                                            a = 0.0                  # safety default
```

**Why this should work better**

- The **0.3 thrust in the 0.40‑0.45 band** is kept (as in the best policy) but is now *conditioned on a positive velocity*, preventing a useless forward push when the car is already sliding back.
- The **0.5 thrust in the 0.35‑0.40 band** gives a little extra “push‑over‑the‑hill” momentum that helped the best runs achieve ~+94 reward.
- The **fallback to 0.0** when the car is already fast near the goal removes the unnecessary ‑0.1 a² penalty that sometimes drags the total reward down.
- All other zones (deep left valley, left‑side braking) are unchanged because they have proven essential.

---

