## Updated policy (the one we will use from now on)

```pseudo
// ---------------------------------------------------------------
//  Mountain‑Car controller – continuous force ∈ [‑1, +1]
// ---------------------------------------------------------------

IF position >= 0.45 THEN
    // Goal reached – stop applying any force
    action = 0.0

ELSE IF position <= -0.20 THEN
    // We are still in the left valley
    IF velocity < 0 THEN
        // Car is moving left – give a modest left push
        // stronger push when we are far left
        IF position < -0.55 THEN
            action = -0.60          // deep left side
        ELSE
            action = -0.45          // nearer the centre
        ENDIF
    ELSE
        // Car already moving right – give a strong right push
        action = 0.90
    ENDIF

ELSE
    // -----------------------------------------------------------
    //  Middle / right‑hand side (‑0.20 < position < 0.45)
    // -----------------------------------------------------------
    dist      = 0.45 - position                 // > 0
    // linear decay of the nominal thrust (max 0.70)
    base      = 0.70 * (dist / (0.45 + 0.20))

    // damp the thrust when we are already fast
    vel_factor = max(0.0, 1.0 - 0.90 * velocity)

    // quadratic taper only in the last 0.10 m
    IF dist <= 0.10 THEN
        taper = (dist / 0.10) ^ 2
    ELSE
        taper = 1.0
    ENDIF

    action = base * vel_factor * taper
ENDIF

// -----------------------------------------------------------
//  Brake‑near‑goal – avoid overshoot when we are already fast
// -----------------------------------------------------------
IF position > 0.42 AND velocity > 0.02 THEN
    // we are very close to the summit and still moving forward:
    // do not allow a positive force any more
    action = min(action, 0.0)
ENDIF

// -----------------------------------------------------------
//  Clip to the legal action range
// -----------------------------------------------------------
action = max(-1.0, min(1.0, action))
```

### Why this policy should be the best so far

| Component | Reason it helps |
|-----------|-----------------|
| **Strong +0.9 thrust while `position > -0.20` and `velocity ≥ 0`** | Quickly builds the kinetic energy needed to climb the right hill. |
| **Modest negative thrust (‑0.45 / ‑0.60) when moving left** | Keeps the “rock‑back‑and‑forth” efficient; the extra magnitude when `position < -0.55` prevents the car from getting stuck far left. |
| **Linear decay (`base = 0.70 * dist/0.65`)** | Guarantees that the force smoothly reduces as we get closer to the goal, avoiding unnecessary large‑action penalties. |
| **Velocity‑damping (`1‑0.90*velocity`)** | The faster we are already moving forward, the less extra push we need – this directly cuts the `‑0.1·a²` penalty. |
| **Quadratic taper inside the last 0.10 m** | Gives a gentle “coast‑to‑stop” behaviour, preventing a hard braking that would waste reward. |
| **Explicit brake clause (`position > 0.42 && velocity > 0.02`)** | Stops the car from overshooting the summit while still respecting the smooth taper; the overshoot penalty is the biggest source of reward loss in the earlier trials. |
| **Clipping** | Guarantees we never ask for an illegal force. |

With this rule‑set the agent reproduces the successful pattern observed in the *previous* strategy (steady increase of position, smooth reduction of thrust, finish exactly at the goal) while adding a few safety tweaks that should raise the average reward even higher than the ≈ 96 we have already seen.

