| **Best so far** | **96.01** | Smaller constant thrust in the valley (0.6) + a gentle quadratic ramp‑down in the last 0.10 m, no explicit “brake‑near‑goal”. | The modest thrust limits the *‑0.1·a²* penalty while still building enough momentum to climb the right hill. The quadratic ramp‑down gives a smooth deceleration exactly when the car is close to the top, so the final step almost always lands on the goal and receives the +100 bonus. | No explicit safety‑brake – if the car happens to be a little faster than expected it can still overshoot, but the overshoot is rare because the ramp‑down is already strong. |

**Take‑away:**  
* The *most important* factor is **how much thrust we give while the car is still deep in the left valley**. Too much (≈ 0.9) inflates the action‑penalty; too little (≈ 0.3) makes the climb take many more steps, also hurting the total reward.  
* A **smooth, quadratic reduction of thrust** once the car is within ≈ 0.1 m of the goal works better than a hard “cut‑to‑zero” brake.  
* Adding a *tiny* negative thrust **only when the car is already past the goal** (or moving too fast right at the top) can recover the occasional overshoot without sacrificing the overall smoothness.

---

### 2️⃣ Updated policy – “Gentle‑Push‑and‑Graceful‑Taper”

Below is a compact set of rules that incorporates the lessons above.  
All arithmetic is done **every time‑step**; the policy is deterministic and uses only the current `(position, velocity)`.

```text
IF position >= 0.45 THEN
    // Goal reached – stay still
    action = 0.0

ELSE IF position <= -0.20 THEN
    // Deep in the left valley: give a moderate push to the right,
    // but still be able to reverse if we are sliding left.
    IF velocity < 0 THEN
        // We are sliding further left – give a stronger left push
        // (helps the car build kinetic energy against the left wall)
        action = -0.70
    ELSE
        action = 0.75          // main forward thrust
    ENDIF

ELSE
    // We are on the right side of the valley, heading to the goal.
    dist      = 0.45 - position                // > 0
    // Base thrust decays linearly from the centre of the valley to the goal.
    base      = 0.65 * (dist / (0.45 + 0.20))

    // Reduce thrust when we are already moving fast forward.
    vel_factor = max(0.0, 1.0 - 0.85 * velocity)

    // Quadratic taper when we get close to the top.
    IF dist <= 0.08 THEN
        taper = (dist / 0.08) ^ 2
    ELSE
        taper = 1.0
    ENDIF

    action = base * vel_factor * taper
ENDIF

/* ---- Gentle correction at the very top --------------------------------- */
IF position > 0.42 AND velocity > 0.02 THEN
    // We are very close to the hill‑top and still moving forward.
    // Apply a *tiny* negative thrust just to bleed off excess speed.
    action = min(action, -0.10)      // never positive here
ENDIF

/* ---- Safety brake if we accidentally cross the goal line --------------- */
IF position > 0.45 AND velocity > 0.0 THEN
    // We have overshot the goal – push left just enough to stop.
    action = -0.30
ENDIF

/* ---- Clip to the legal action range ------------------------------------ */
action = max(-1.0, min(1.0, action))
```

#### Why this should beat the previous best (≈ 96)

| Component | Expected effect |
|-----------|-----------------|
| **Moderate forward thrust (≈ 0.75) in the left valley** | Keeps the *action‑penalty* low (‑0.1·0.75² ≈ ‑0.056) while still providing enough kinetic energy to climb the right hill in ≈ 40 steps. |
| **Stronger left‑push (‑0.70) when sliding left** | Guarantees the car does not get “stuck” at the far left wall; the extra negative thrust is paid only when the velocity is already negative, so the net penalty is small. |
| **Linear base + velocity‑factor** | Prevents the policy from “wasting” thrust when the car is already fast, reducing unnecessary penalty. |
| **Quadratic taper (dist ≤ 0.08)** | Produces a very smooth deceleration in the last 0.08 m, almost guaranteeing that the final step lands exactly at `position >= 0.45` and therefore receives the +100 bonus. |
| **Tiny corrective negative thrust (`‑0.10`) near the top** | If the car is still a bit fast, this small brake removes only a fraction of the kinetic energy (penalty ≈ ‑0.001) but prevents an overshoot, so the +100 is kept. |
| **Explicit overshoot‑brake (`‑0.30`)** | Handles the rare case where the car crosses the goal line with a sizable forward speed; the penalty is outweighed by the guaranteed +100. |

All together the policy keeps the *average per‑step penalty* well below 0.06 while still reaching the goal in ~ 45 steps, which translates to an **expected total reward of ≈ 96.5–97** (slightly higher than the previous best 96.01).

