## 2️⃣  Revised “most‑effective” policy  

Below is a compact, self‑contained pseudo‑code that incorporates the three ingredients that proved to work best:

```pseudo
// ------------------------------------------------------------
//  Mountain‑Car controller – “soft‑landing” policy
// ------------------------------------------------------------
IF position >= 0.45 THEN
    // Goal reached – stop applying force
    action = 0.0

ELSE IF position <= -0.20 THEN
    // Deep in the left valley → build momentum
    IF velocity < 0 THEN
        // Car is still sliding backwards → push it left a bit
        IF position < -0.55 THEN
            action = -0.45          // stronger left thrust when very far left
        ELSE
            action = -0.30
        ENDIF
    ELSE
        // Already moving right → give a strong forward thrust
        action = 0.60
    ENDIF

ELSE
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // 1)  Distance‑based nominal push (linear decay)
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    dist      = 0.45 - position                     // >0 while we are left of the goal
    basePush  = 0.60 * (dist / 0.65)                // 0.65 = 0.45 (goal) + 0.20 (left‑bound)

    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // 2)  Dampen when we are already fast enough
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    velFactor = max(0.0, 1.0 - 0.80 * velocity)    // 0 ≤ velFactor ≤ 1

    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // 3)  Quadratic taper in the last 0.10 m
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    IF dist <= 0.10 THEN
        taper = (dist / 0.10) ^ 2                  // 0 → 1 smoothly
    ELSE
        taper = 1.0
    ENDIF

    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // 4)  Preliminary action (no brake yet)
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    action = basePush * velFactor * taper

    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // 5)  Fine‑tuning / soft‑brake on the right slope
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    IF position > 0.35 AND velocity > 0.02 THEN
        excess   = velocity - 0.02                // how much faster than the “ideal” speed
        brake    = - min(0.12, 5.0 * excess)      // linear brake, capped at -0.12
        action   = action + brake
    ENDIF
ENDIF

// --------------------------------------------------------
// Clip to the legal action range [-1, +1]
// --------------------------------------------------------
action = max(-1.0, min(1.0, action))
```

