## 3. Updated policy (pseudo‑code)  

Below is the **final rule‑set** that combines the successful ingredients and removes the wasteful parts.  
It is written in the same “IF … THEN … ENDIF” style you have been using, so you can drop it directly into your controller.

```text
// ------------------------------------------------------------
// Mountain‑Car policy – maximise +100 reward, minimise -0.1*a²
// ------------------------------------------------------------

IF position >= 0.45 THEN
    // Goal reached – no more thrust needed
    action = 0.0

ELSE IF position <= -0.20 THEN
    // Left side of the valley – build momentum
    // A constant forward push of 0.60 works best
    action = 0.60

ELSE
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    //  Right side (between -0.20 and the goal)
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    dist        = 0.45 - position                // positive distance left
    maxDist     = 0.65                           // total span from -0.20 to goal
    base        = 0.60 * (dist / maxDist)        // linear decay with distance

    // Quadratic soft‑landing when we are within 0.10 m of the top
    IF dist <= 0.10 THEN
        base = base * (dist / 0.10) ^ 2          // ramp‑down ∝ (dist)²
    ENDIF

    // Dampen the thrust when we are already moving fast forward
    vel_factor  = max(0.0, 1.0 - 0.8 * velocity) // 0 ≤ vel_factor ≤ 1

    // Combine the pieces
    action = base * vel_factor

    // Final tiny nudge – guarantee crossing the exact goal line
    IF dist <= 0.02 AND velocity < 0.02 THEN
        action = action + (0.02 - velocity)      // add just enough forward push
    ENDIF
ENDIF

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// Safety: keep action inside the allowed interval [-1, 1]
// ------------------------------------------------------------
action = max(-1.0, min(1.0, action))
```

### Why this version should be the best

* **Momentum building** – a steady 0.60 N thrust on the left side is enough to climb out of the valley while keeping the per‑step penalty low (`-0.1 * 0.6² ≈ -0.036`).  
* **Smooth deceleration** – the linear decay + quadratic taper makes the thrust shrink automatically as the car approaches the hill top, so the velocity naturally falls to ≈ 0.02 m/s right before the goal.  
* **Velocity‑aware damping** – the term `1‑0.8·velocity` removes any unnecessary thrust once the car is already moving forward fast, further reducing the action penalty.  
